# Veripsa release gate (auto-discovered). One gate per file -> two PRs adding gates add two FILES, never a
# shared line -> no false merge conflict on registration. register_gate is defined in run_gates.sh.
# Format: register_gate <test> <marker> <name> <ok_blurb> <desc> [tail]
# NOTE: NO backticks and NO dollar-sign in the desc/blurb text below (shell-eval fragility -- see CLAUDE.md).
register_gate "tests/test_pause_comment_wording.py" "PAUSE COMMENT WORDING GATE: PASS" "pause comment wording (kill the paused-vs-advisory contradiction, always show PR refs in the land order, clear-head no longer reads as paused, no double Wait-in-line)" "pause comment wording: the customer-facing PR-comment WORDING the pause-and-ack tier left self-contradictory on live prod PRs (verbatim from prod comments) -- a genuinely-grounded analysis read hollow because the copy fought itself. WORDING/RENDER only (render.py): no verdict-logic change, no pause/ack-mechanism change, content-free throughout (paths, PR/branch refs, counts -- never file bodies), no internal jargon, no overclaim. FOUR defects fixed on the REAL render_pr_check / apply_pause_ack output. P1 CONTRADICTION: a PAUSED PR (verdict serialize -> check action_required) showed the pause banner (Veripsa paused this -- to proceed add the veripsa-ack label) AND, lower in the SAME comment, the stale parenthetical (Advisory -- the order is a suggestion, not a block.). A paused check is NOT just advisory / not a block -- that line was leftover from the pre-pause-ack era and flatly contradicted the pause; the queued-behind block likewise denied blocking (Advisory -- nothing is blocked.) and the split-advice block (never a block.). FIX: those inner block-denials are removed from the serialize/holder body; the honest, non-contradicting FOOTER (Advisory by default; your branch-protection policy decides what blocks) STAYS on every comment and carries the advisory frame once, correctly, whether or not the PR is in the pause tier. P2 AUTHOR COLLAPSE in the suggested land order: several PRs by ONE author rendered as 1. example-user / 2. example-user / ... -- bare-author noise, some entries with NO PR ref at all (a BR- branch push not yet reconciled to a PR renders author-name-only). FIX: every suggested-order entry now carries its content-free PR/branch ref (PR-n / BR-x), recovered from the engine per-change rows by a label-to-ref map, so a same-author cluster reads PR-1, PR-2, PR-10, PR-11 and no row is ever a bare author with no ref (a degraded unrecoverable row falls back to a generic placeholder, never a nameless author). P3 CLEAR/HEAD: the PR at the HEAD of a contention cluster (own verdict clear/success -- first in line, clear to land) must NOT read as paused -- its header must say clear-to-land while others wait behind it (this was ALREADY correct on current main: is_material_coupling is false for clear, so apply_pause_ack leaves it success and the header is Clear to land; the gate LOCKS that so a future change cannot regress a clear head into a wait-in-line / paused banner). P4 DOUBLE HEADLINE: Wait in line appeared TWICE -- the bold comment header AND the body block (Wait in line. ...). FIX: the serialize body block now leads with the ACTION (Land in order.) instead of re-stating the header, so the phrase appears once. Proven PURE/offline on the REAL render_pr_check + apply_pause_ack with a same-author cluster whose suggested_order MIXES a ref-carrying label and an author-only BR- label (the live prod shape): (1) a paused serialize PR carries no order-is-a-suggestion-not-a-block / nothing-is-blocked / never-a-block denial of the pause yet keeps the branch-protection-decides-what-blocks footer; (2) every land-order entry carries a PR/BR ref incl. the recovered author-only one; (3) a clear cluster-head is success / not-material with a Clear to land header and no pause banner; (4) Wait in line appears at most once and the body leads with Land in order. Keeps the no-jargon, render-honesty and overclaim gates green" "pause comment wording: a paused PR no longer says both this-is-paused-ack-to-proceed and this-is-only-advisory-not-a-block in the same comment (the contradicting inner parentheticals are gone, the honest branch-protection-decides footer stays); every suggested land-order entry now carries its content-free PR/branch ref so a same-author cluster reads PR-1, PR-2, PR-10, PR-11 not example-user, example-user, ...; a clear cluster-head reads clear-to-land not paused; and Wait in line appears once not twice. WORDING/RENDER only, content-free, verdict + pause mechanism unchanged" 24
